        <!-- ===================== §4 · THE FIRST 72 HOURS ===================== -->
        <section class="sec" id="first72">
          <h2>The First Seventy-Two Hours After Your Bird Lands</h2>
          <p class="opener">Our written guarantee runs 72 hours from arrival, with a separate 24-hour clause for anything caused by the journey. It is short on purpose, and we would rather explain why than let a longer number do the persuading.</p>
          <img class="sec-img inf-img" src={IMG + "first-72-hours-after-african-grey-arrives-infographic.webp"}
               srcset={IMG + "first-72-hours-after-african-grey-arrives-infographic-760.webp 760w, " + IMG + "first-72-hours-after-african-grey-arrives-infographic.webp 1408w"}
               sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 760px" width="1408" height="768" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
               alt="Four steps covered by the seventy-two hour health guarantee after arrival">

          <h3>The 72-Hour Guarantee, Stated Plainly</h3>
          <p>Three days from the moment your bird reaches you, an examination by your own avian vet decides the question, and the remedy is replacement or refund. Book the appointment before the bird travels, because good avian practices run a waiting list and the window does not pause while you find one.</p>
          <img class="sec-img inf-img" src={IMG + "the-seventy-two-hour-guarantee-stated-plainly-infographic.webp"}
               srcset={IMG + "the-seventy-two-hour-guarantee-stated-plainly-infographic-760.webp 760w, " + IMG + "the-seventy-two-hour-guarantee-stated-plainly-infographic.webp 1408w"}
               sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 760px" width="1408" height="768" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
               alt="The written guarantee window counted plainly across three arrival days">

          <h3>Is a Longer Guarantee a Better Guarantee?</h3>
          <p>Usually the opposite. A year-long promise sounds generous precisely because almost nobody expects to be asked to honour it, and the sellers advertising the longest windows in our search were the ones we could verify least. A short window that names its terms is worth more than a long one that names none.</p>
          <img class="sec-img inf-img" src={IMG + "is-a-longer-guarantee-a-better-guarantee-infographic.webp"}
               srcset={IMG + "is-a-longer-guarantee-a-better-guarantee-infographic-760.webp 760w, " + IMG + "is-a-longer-guarantee-a-better-guarantee-infographic.webp 1408w"}
               sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 760px" width="1408" height="768" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
               alt="A short enforceable promise set against a long vague one">

          <h4>What Makes a Health Guarantee Enforceable?</h4>
          <p>Four things: it is in writing, it names an independent vet as the arbiter, it states a time limit, and it states the remedy. Ours does all four and <a href="/african-grey-parrot-health-guarantee/">the full policy</a> carries the wording. A guarantee missing any of them is a sentiment rather than a term.</p>
          <img class="sec-img inf-img" src={IMG + "what-makes-a-health-guarantee-enforceable-infographic.webp"}
               srcset={IMG + "what-makes-a-health-guarantee-enforceable-infographic-760.webp 760w, " + IMG + "what-makes-a-health-guarantee-enforceable-infographic.webp 1408w"}
               sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 760px" width="1408" height="768" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
               alt="Four clauses that make a bird health guarantee possible to enforce">

          <h5>A Guarantee Is Worth Exactly as Much as the Address Behind It</h5>
          <p>Any document is only as good as your ability to find the people who wrote it. We are a licensed aviary at a verifiable address with a phone number in the footer, which is the part that makes the rest of it mean anything.</p>

          <h6>On the Paperwork: What Ours Says, Word for Word</h6>
          <p>Seventy-two hours from arrival for health, twenty-four for transit, confirmed by your own avian veterinarian, settled as replacement or refund, void on removing the leg ring or on skipping the examination. The document identifies your bird by the ring number rather than by its name, which is why <a href="#papers">the paperwork section</a> matters more than it looks.</p>
